  "Number": 1,
  "Question": "One can holds \\(12\\) ounces of soda. What is the minimum number of cans needed to provide a gallon (\\(128\\) ounces) of soda?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(7\\)",
    "B": "\\(8\\)",
    "C": "\\(9\\)",
    "D": "\\(10\\)",
    "E": "\\(11\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Divide the required amount by the amount in one can:\n\\[\n128=12\\cdot10+8.\n\\]\nTen cans provide only \\(120\\) ounces, leaving \\(8\\) ounces still needed. One additional can supplies enough, since eleven cans contain \\(12\\cdot11=132\\) ounces. Thus the minimum is \\(\\boxed{11}\\) cans, choice \\(\\mathrm{E}\\).",
